   "widgets_values": [
    "## Qwen-Image 2.1 Image Edit + LanPaint, with a mask and with transparency\n\nThe official `Qwen Image 2.1 Image Edit` template with a mask bolted on. The instruction\nrefers to the two pictures as `<image1>` (the one being edited) and `<image2>` (the material\nbeing borrowed).\n\nOnly what you paint over changes - everything outside the mask is anchored to the original on\nevery step, so the headband, the stitching and the hinges come back untouched rather than\nmerely similar.\n\nThe picture's transparency is edited along with its colours, so the rebuilt part can grow a\nnew outline over what used to be empty background. The mask is a separate greyscale file,\nwhite = edit here, and it is deliberately larger than the earcups so the new shape has room\nto flare out."
   ],
   "title": "How this works",
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  }
